# CODEOWNERS — routes review of a pull request to the person answerable for a file.
# Infrastructure, not knowledge (SKILL.md §1.4). Replace the placeholders with real
# GitHub handles or delete the lines you do not need; an unmatched path simply gets
# no automatic reviewer.
#
# Rule from _rules/governance.md §5: a protocol change and a content change never
# travel in the same pull request, because they have different reviewers.

# --- Protocol: the rules of the game. Highest scrutiny. ---
/SKILL.md                 @OWNER
/AGENTS.md                @OWNER
/PROTOCOL-CHANGELOG.md    @OWNER
/_meta/                   @OWNER
/_rules/                  @OWNER
/_templates/              @OWNER
/_tools/                  @OWNER
/_tests/                  @OWNER
/_install/                @OWNER
/.github/                 @OWNER

# --- Global map: touched by almost every change, review it deliberately. ---
/INDEX.md                 @OWNER

# --- Knowledge: one owner per project. Mirror the `owner` front matter. ---
# /<project-slug>/         @PROJECT-OWNER
# /<project-slug>/_data/   @DATA-OWNER
